.TH TOPTOP 1 "2026" "toptop 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
toptop \- a gorgeous, feature-rich terminal system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B toptop
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B toptop
is an htop/btop-class terminal system monitor written in Rust. It displays
CPU (global and per-core), memory and swap, per-interface network throughput,
per-mount disk usage and I/O, GPU (NVIDIA, AMD, Intel), temperature sensors and
battery, alongside an interactive process table with tree view, live filtering,
per-process I/O rates, a signal menu, and a network-connections inspector.
.PP
Graphs are drawn with high-resolution braille cells and meters use truecolor
gradients. Five themes are included and the layout adapts from a wide desktop
terminal down to a tiny pane.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tick " " \fIMS\fR
Refresh interval in milliseconds (100\(en60000).
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fINAME\fR
Color theme: \fIgruvbox\fR, \fInord\fR, \fIdracula\fR, \fItokyonight\fR, \fImatrix\fR, \fIcyberpunk\fR, or \fIpaper\fR (for light terminals).
.TP
.B \-\-tree
Start in process-tree view.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tree
Start in flat process view.
.TP
.B \-\-ai
Open the AI / local-LLM GPU view on launch.
.TP
.BR \-\-export " " \fIFMT\fR
Print metrics and exit (no TUI): \fIjson\fR (default) or \fIprometheus\fR
(Prometheus exposition format for Grafana/VictoriaMetrics).
.TP
.BR \-\-serve\-metrics " " [\fIADDR\fR]
Run a long-running Prometheus metrics endpoint (default \fI127.0.0.1:9709\fR),
serving \fB/metrics\fR for continuous scraping. Includes \fBtoptop_alert\fR
gauges for VRAM-spill, GPU-throttle, KV-cache and queue-backlog conditions.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Use an explicit config file instead of the default location.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save
Don't write the config back on exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-alert\-vram " " \fIPCT\fR
VRAM usage percentage that triggers the spill-risk alert (default 90).
.TP
.BR \-\-alert\-kv " " \fIPCT\fR
KV-cache usage percentage considered saturated (default 95).
.TP
.BR \-\-alert\-queue " " \fIN\fR
Number of queued requests considered a backlog (default 8).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-themes
Print available themes and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot
Print a one-shot text snapshot and exit (no TUI).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.BR \[ua] / \[da] ", " k / j
Move selection.
.TP
.BR PgUp / PgDn
Page up / down.
.TP
.BR Home / End ", " g / G
Jump to first / last.
.TP
.B Enter
Toggle the process detail view.
.TP
.B a
Toggle the AI / local-LLM GPU view: utilization vs. memory bandwidth, VRAM
headroom, per-process VRAM, throttle, multi-GPU aggregate, auto-discovered
inference-server metrics (tokens/sec, KV cache, queue, TTFT) scraped from
llama.cpp/vLLM/TGI/Ollama, and serving/training workload detection.
.TP
.B n
Open the network-connections inspector.
.TP
.B s
Cycle the sort column; \fBi\fR inverts the order.
.TP
.B t
Toggle the process tree.
.TP
.B e
Toggle per-core CPU meters.
.TP
.B L
Cycle the layout preset (full / cpu / process).
.TP
.B /
Filter processes as you type.
.TP
.BR K / F9
Open the signal menu; \fBDel\fR sends SIGTERM, \fBx\fR sends SIGKILL.
.TP
.BR p / P
Next / previous theme.
.TP
.BR + / \-
Faster / slower refresh.
.TP
.B space
Pause / resume.
.TP
.BR ? / F1
Toggle the help overlay.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/toptop/config.conf
Persisted settings (theme, refresh interval, tree mode, layout, alert
thresholds: \fBalert_vram_pct\fR, \fBalert_kv_pct\fR, \fBalert_queue\fR).
Honors
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ;
overridden by
.BR \-\-config .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and 2 on an invalid command-line argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR htop (1),
.BR top (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The toptop authors. Source: https://github.com/ur-grue/toptop
